    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] He began his career on the stage, and in 1994 made his film debut in the Bong Joon-ho short film \"Baeksekin\" (\"White Man\" or \"White-collar worker\"), followed by Jang Sun-woo's \"Bad Movie\" in 1997.\n[2] It is also the directorial debut of Bong Joon-ho, who would later go on to direct \"Memories of Murder\" in 2003, \"The Host\" in 2006, and \"Snowpiercer\" in 2013.\n[3] The film marks Bong's English-language debut; approximately 80% of the film was shot in English.\n[4] Shim became notable when he co-wrote \"Memories of Murder\" with director Bong Joon-ho in 2003."
